# Sweep along a cubic (roadmap 20): with the cubic of a 3d sketch picked,
# Sweep Along Path moves the active sketch's rectangle along it, its
# surface fitted; the group screen lists the path, the twist and how the
# frames turn. Analyze > Check Solid finds it sound; a twist of 90
# degrees typed in turns the far end, still sound. Holding the frames to
# z is a problem, since the path starts along z; held to x the sweep is
# sound; undo twice lets them turn least again.
file $testdata/ui/sweep_cubic.tlspr
menu File|Open...
view default
move 382.5 232.5
down L 382.5 232.5
up L 382.5 232.5
menu Features|Sweep Along Path
dump
tw
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
twmove 154 165
twdown L 154 165
twup L 154 165
edit 90
tw
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
twmove 397 205
twdown L 397 205
twup L 397 205
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
tw
twmove 235 205
twdown L 235 205
twup L 235 205
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
key z ctrl
key z ctrl
tw
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
